  "numId": 55,
  "title": "Single-Digit BCD Adder (A + B)",
  "description": "Design a single-digit BCD adder that adds two BCD digits A (A3 A2 A1 A0) and B (B3 B2 B1 B0), each in the range 0-9. Inputs A and B are mapped to Switches 0-3 and Switches 4-7 respectively. The circuit must produce a valid BCD sum S (S3 S2 S1 S0) and a BCD carry-out Cout. Use two 7483 ICs and basic gates. Hint: after the first binary addition, the result must be corrected by adding 6 (0110) whenever the sum exceeds 9. The correction condition is Cout = K + Z3.Z2 + Z3.Z1, where K is the carry-out of the first adder and Z3 Z2 Z1 Z0 is its sum.",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "design",
